+# Maintaining Cloudflare OS overlay changes
+
+This tree incorporates downstream extensions for Cloudflare OS maintained through the [cloudflare-os-overlay](https://github.com/dscott98/cloudflare-os-overlay) repository.
+
+## Overlay architecture
+
+Rather than maintaining a diverging, long-lived Git fork of Cloudflare OS, downstream customizations are maintained as an ordered, checksum-verified patch series (`patches/*.patch`) pinned to an immutable upstream commit SHA (`UPSTREAM.json`).
+
+## Maintenance workflow
+
+The overlay repository (`cloudflare-os-overlay`) provides an automated workflow to verify, update, and release downstream patches:
+
+### 1. Upstream pin
+`UPSTREAM.json` records the exact pinned commit of `https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-os.git`.
+
+### 2. Patch series
+The `patches/` directory contains ordered `git format-patch` files:
+- `0001-feat-add-deployment-AI-Gateway-custom-models.patch`
+- `0002-feat-allow-native-AI-Gateway-provider-routes.patch`
+- `0003-docs-add-fork-maintenance-and-gadget-review.patch`
+- `0004-fix-hide-deployment-model-editor-without-gateway.patch`
+- `0005-feat-move-deployment-AI-Gateway-model-setup-into-add-dialog.patch`
+
+Integrity is guaranteed by `PATCHES.sha256`.
+
+### 3. Verification
+In the overlay repository, run:
+```bash
+git submodule update --init --recursive
+./scripts/verify-release.sh
+```
+This script creates a clean detached worktree at the pinned upstream commit, verifies patch SHA-256 checksums, applies the patch series, and executes the full workspace type checks, linter, and test suite.
+
+### 4. Applying patches to a target checkout
+To apply the overlay to an external clean clone of Cloudflare OS:
+```bash
+./scripts/apply-patches.sh /path/to/clean/cloudflare-os
+```
+
+### 5. Updating to a newer upstream commit
+When updating the upstream pin:
+1. Fetch latest changes from `https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-os.git`.
+2. Check out the proposed upstream SHA in a clean worktree.
+3. Apply `patches/*.patch` using `git am --3way`.
+4. If conflicts occur, resolve them and regenerate the updated patch series:
+   ```bash
+   git format-patch <upstream-sha> --output-directory /path/to/cloudflare-os-overlay/patches
+   ```
+5. Run workspace linting, type checks, and tests.
+6. Update `UPSTREAM.json`, `RELEASES.md`, the submodule pointer, and `PATCHES.sha256`.
+7. Re-run `./scripts/verify-release.sh` to confirm full release candidate verification.
