+
+## Test plan
+
+- Admin authorization: non-admin callers cannot obtain the admin capability or mutate the catalog.
+- Config persistence: defaults, malformed/legacy config, create/edit/delete, and KV-mirror failure
+  behavior.
+- Validation: blank, oversized, malformed, duplicate, and path-special slug/model/endpoint values.
+- Visibility: every user lists shared models; personal direct/BYOK models remain visible only to
+  their owner; deleted shared entries disappear.
+- Identity: same raw model ID can coexist across two custom providers and with a personal model;
+  user model creation cannot claim the reserved shared-ID namespace.
+- Resolution: opaque shared IDs resolve to the intended slug/model; stale chat IDs fail clearly and
+  never fall through to a personal model.
+- Routing: a shared custom model uses the deployment gateway route and credentials, never Workers
+  AI or a direct endpoint; verify `v1` and `v4` endpoint paths, encoded path segments, request API
+  shape, headers, and gateway log route.
+- PDFs: custom models accept, replay, and send the expected `application/pdf` data URL through
+  Chat Completions. A rejecting provider surfaces its response error; no alternative PDF dialect is
+  silently substituted.
+- Billing precedence: cover the policy selected above for a user with a connected personal
+  Cloudflare account.
+- Frontend: admin CRUD states/errors and regular-user read-only presentation.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- An admin can create, edit, and delete a deployment-wide custom-provider model entry.
+- A non-admin cannot mutate it through the UI or a crafted RPC call.
+- Every user can select the entry without entering an upstream API key.
+- The request reaches the configured deployment AI Gateway custom provider using its
+  OpenAI-compatible contract, not Workers AI.
+- Two entries can use identical upstream model IDs when their provider slugs differ.
+- Existing per-user direct/BYOK models continue to work unchanged.
+- Removing an entry does not cause an old chat to select or execute a different model.
